/target

# Cargo.lock IS committed: CI must resolve the exact batteries-included graph
# (the always-compiled zlib/LZO/zstd decoders) rather than a fresh resolution
# that could pull a license-tainted or edition-incompatible transitive. The lock
# also backs the CI freshness gate. (Downstream library consumers still resolve
# their own graph — a committed lock does not constrain them.)

# The large minted btrfs oracle image is gitignored (512 MiB) — only the small
# extracted superblock fixture (btrfs_superblock.bin) and the oracle TEXT
# outputs / provenance are committed. Re-mint from the recorded mkfs commands.
/tests/data/*.img

# The Tier-1 real-world corpus (downloaded Fedora Cloud qcow2 + the extracted
# btrfs partition raw) is large (~469 MB) and freely re-downloadable — never
# committed. The env-gated tier1_fedora test reads it on demand via
# BTRFS_FEDORA_ORACLE; provenance is recorded in tests/data/README.md.
*.qcow2
/tests/data/fedora-btrfs.raw
/tests/data/fedora.raw

# OS / editor cruft (belt-and-suspenders alongside a machine-wide core.excludesfile).
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
